{#
  SDC-SPEC-EGRESS-v2.0 :: SOVEREIGN DECLARATIVE EGRESS CONTRACT
  CANONICAL ARTIFACT RENDERER — SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH (SSOT)
  Paired with SDC-SPEC-INGRESS-v3.1.json's "init" stage.

  REVISION NOTE: 'v2.0' is this TEMPLATE DOCUMENT's own revision number,
  decoupled from 'contract_version' inside the paired .json file -- see
  that file's _readme, directive 2, for why the two numbers are tracked
  separately.

  ARCHITECTURE DIRECTIVE:
  Governs the deterministic transformation of internal canonical state into
  a syntax-immune, enterprise-grade JSON egress artifact.

  STRICT RENDER RULES (ZERO-EXCEPTION GOVERNANCE):

  1. SYNTAX IMMUNITY: 100% of rendered values MUST pipe through `| tojson`,
     no exceptions -- including values you're sure are "just a number".
     This is what makes the output valid JSON regardless of embedded
     quotes, backslashes, or non-ASCII text; it directly eliminates
     structural JSON corruption at runtime.

  2. STRICT-UNDEFINED SAFETY: every OPTIONAL attribute is rendered as
     `{{ field | default(none) | tojson }}` -- `default(none)` first,
     `tojson` second, always in that order. The engine's Jinja Environment
     runs under StrictUndefined: a field genuinely ABSENT from render
     context (not just null-valued) raises without this filter -- a
     controlled boundary halt rather than silent data corruption.

  3. DETERMINISTIC ROW ORDINALS: `loop.index0` (`row_index`) is stamped
     into every fanned-out element, unconditionally -- the tiebreaker that
     keeps a compound key unique even when every other component collides.

  4. VOCABULARY ISOLATION: raw status codes and rendered display labels
     are decoupled via STATUS_LABELS. Any DECISION_MATRIX rule reading a
     rendered field back must compare against the LABEL side, never the
     raw backend code -- the two vocabularies must never be conflated.

  5. FILTER IDEMPOTENCY: domain-specific structural filters (as_link_field,
     as_user_field, from filters/structural_filters.py) already return
     null / [] on empty input by design -- do NOT wrap them in an
     additional `| default(none)`. That would suppress the filter's own
     "empty" encoding in favor of a generic one, and the two are not
     guaranteed to match a given destination system's convention.

  PUBLIC ARTIFACT NOTICE: shareable outside the private repo. No real
  customer_id, credentials, or case-study-identifying field names. A
  forked copy used for a real contract becomes an IP Vault artifact again
  and should NOT be published as-is.
#}
{%- set STATUS_LABELS = {
  "OPEN": "Open",
  "CLOSED": "Closed",
  "CANCELLED": "Cancelled",
  "ARCHIVED": "Archived"
} -%}
{%- set TERMINAL_STATUS_SET = ["CLOSED", "CANCELLED", "ARCHIVED"] -%}
{%- set status_label = STATUS_LABELS.get(status, status) -%}
{%- set is_terminal_status = status in TERMINAL_STATUS_SET -%}
[
{%- for row in line_items | default([{}]) %}
  {
    "record_id": {{ record_id | tojson }},
    "record_link": {{ record_id | as_link_field | tojson }},
    "row_index": {{ loop.index0 | tojson }},
    "status": {{ status_label | tojson }},
    "owner_id": {{ owner_id | as_user_field | tojson }},

    "label": {{ label | default(none) | tojson }},

{%- if not is_terminal_status %}
    "note": {{ note | default(none) | tojson }},
    "amount": {{ amount | default(none) | tojson }},
    "amount_currency": {{ amount_currency | default(none) | tojson }},

    "item_code": {{ row.get("item_code") | default(none) | tojson }},
    "item_qty": {{ row.get("item_qty") | default(none) | tojson }},
    "item_amount": {{ row.get("item_amount") | default(none) | tojson }},
    "item_amount-Currency": {{ row.get("item_amount-Currency") | default(none) | tojson }},
{%- endif %}

    "instance_code": {{ instance_code | default(none) | tojson }},
    "created_at": {{ created_at | default(none) | tojson }},
    "updated_at": {{ updated_at | default(none) | tojson }},

    "report_window_start": {{ current_timestamp | shift_days(-7) | to_date_str | tojson }},
    "report_window_end": {{ current_timestamp | to_date_str | tojson }}
  }{{ "," if not loop.last }}
{%- endfor %}
]
